task: frontend-spec
agent: fable-frontend
started: 2026-09-09
branch: feature/frontend-spec
worktree: ../okay-wt-frontend
spec: specs/frontend.md (draft, this claim writes it)

why: the operator's direction (2026-09-09): okay's frontend support
  must be ideal — the logic of a frontend defined by the structure of
  the application, not by the rendering technology; and a DYNAMIC
  native frontend, where the client is as dumb as a browser and the
  server changes all logic without a client update, over a protocol
  that depends on neither side. Answers given: thin clients in the
  platform's own language count (Scala hosts still out of the box);
  two vocabulary levels, semantic and layout, both first-class; hybrid
  from the start — no round trip per keystroke.

what: the spec only — the protocol as a first-class artifact (hello /
  vocab negotiation, lowering on the server, Submitted as the form's
  one typed event, the closed Local set), the staged plan, the laws
  each stage must prove. No code in this claim; each stage is its own
  claim later.

predict: most of specs/ui.md survives unchanged; what changes is the
  wire (a handshake, lowering, Submitted) and the tree (Box with
  weights, style tokens, Image, Scroll, Form/List/Table/Tabs/Modal).
